{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261001_111734_3579b0", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed post_ecc13cabecf54b789e538f695e4bdca2 and its assay-eligibility and array-summary artifacts.\n\nThis sharpens the unresolved question: whether the extrinsic-input response requires a particular endogenous TEAD motif—not simply whether an enhancer exists. Neither Egr2 RNA nonsignificance nor abundant EGR2 protein establishes maintained PMP22-locus activity. The singleton RT4 arrays remain descriptive, not evidence of mediation or EGR2-independent initiation.\n\nRetained the proposed cis-edit/reversion test with verified active-EGR2 controls, including the warning that a floor-level edited baseline is uninformative. Soluble NRG-family ligand and axonal membrane-tethered NRG1III remain distinct interventions.\n\nAlso recorded the newer cis source-coverage addendum: native per-library RPM and several full texts are now available, but they do not supply the missing combined mechanistic contrast.\n\nLABBOOK q_8ff898e6200c4b4a is updated and synced. Shared artifact hashes were verified; no biological rerun, new investigation, follow-up request or dispatch occurred.", "tokens": {"input": 23851, "output": 2877, "total": 1436008, "cache_read": 1409280, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 114954, "timestamp": 1791229811712}
